<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tashkent Declaration</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1966</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indo-pakistani-war-of-1965">Indo-Pakistani War of 1965</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Tashkent</a> Declaration was the peace agreement signed on 10 January 1966 by Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lal-bahadur-shastri">Lal Bahadur Shastri</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayub-khan">Ayub Khan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> at Tashkent, with Soviet mediation by Alexei Kosygin. It ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indo-pakistani-war-of-1965">Indo-Pakistani War of 1965</a> by committing both sides to withdraw to their pre-war positions and restore normal relations. Shastri died of a heart attack in Tashkent the following night.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tashkent-declaration.jpg" alt="Tashkent Declaration" width="320" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fotograaf Onbekend / Anefo · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ayub_Khan_(ex-president_Pakistan),_Ayub_Khan_(links)_en_Kosygin,_Bestanddeelnr_925-3209.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
